<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 2.x Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="_Toc235450425" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 2 — External URLs</title>
   <refbody>
      <section id="sec_d167e7">
         <p>Consider a <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> element that contains an <codeph>&lt;a href="..."&gt;</codeph> element pointing to an external URL.</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Internal link</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_vsc_2sn_lkc">
&lt;p>
  See
  &lt;a href="https://example.com/release-notes">
    the release notes
  &lt;/a>
  for details.
&lt;/p></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock id="codeblock_fqm_2sn_lkc">
&lt;p>
  See
  &lt;xref
    href="https://example.com/release-notes"
    format="html"
    scope="external">
    the release notes
  &lt;/xref>
  for details.
&lt;/p></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
         <p><b>Result:</b> External hyperlinks are preserved. The <codeph>href</codeph> attribute receives the URL, scope="external" is added, and the format attribute is set based on the URL file extension or target type. The element content receives the visible link text.</p>
      </section>
   </refbody>
</reference>
